WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.430
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.160
between Burger King in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.073
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.300
Here's everything you can find on the menu

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.580
at the Burger King in
Japan but not in the US.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.610
Here's everything you can
find at a US Burger King

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.470
you cannot get in Japan.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.180
All right, so let's start
with exclusive burgers.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.640
So, here we have teriyaki lettuce burger

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.738
and teriyaki Whopper.

00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:35.820
Ooh!

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.410
Huge.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.318
Next we have avocado salad burger

00:00:41.318 --> 00:00:43.009
and avocado Whopper.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:46.920
Aah, a little cute baby.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.260
Look at this.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.502
And Whopper.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.820
It's totally different.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.880
This one is so huge.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.047
And avocados, tomato,

00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:01.571
no tomatoes.

00:01:01.571 --> 00:01:02.760
I don't know why.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.470
Next we have quattro cheese Whopper.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:09.865
Oh, big boy.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.830
We've got smoky barbecue Whopper

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.830
and smoky barbecue Whopper junior.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:20.123
And here is spicy Whopper.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:24.951
Ooh!

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:25.992
It's hot sauce.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.757
Next, we have tartar chicken burger.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.598
Ooh, it's got

00:01:33.598 --> 00:01:35.989
a lot of tartar sauce,

00:01:35.989 --> 00:01:38.322
chicken, crispy.

00:01:38.322 --> 00:01:40.980
Burger King in Japan just
released a brand-new burger

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.330
called Guilty Burger.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.950
It's basically butter burger.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:46.850
Why?

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.560
What have you done?

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.830
Let's check out this Guilty
butter beef burger first.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.263
The bun is different.

00:01:54.263 --> 00:01:56.321
Itadakimasu!

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.160
Just a little bit of butter flavor,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.400
but I don't feel as guilty as it claims.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.540
This one is Guilty butter
croquette sandwich.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.540
Ooh.

00:02:10.557 --> 00:02:12.040
Guilty!

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.443
And here is Guilty butter chicken burger.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.005
First one is something
that BK has exclu --

00:02:22.005 --> 00:02:23.930
oh, my God.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.963
This is called the Texas Whopper.

00:02:27.876 --> 00:02:30.351
Look at the size of this f---ing thing.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.230
Two patties, cheese,
bacon, bunch of veggies.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.423
Wait for it!

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.650
The triple Whopper.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.370
Look at the size of this thing.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:48.080
The weight of it has completely
flattened the bottom bun.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.496
And there's nothing between
the patties of meat!

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.030
What the hell are you
guys doing over there?

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.355
Next.

00:02:56.355 --> 00:02:57.650
Oh, the Bacon King.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:58.966
Oh, my God.

00:02:58.966 --> 00:03:02.299
Looks to be pretty bacon centric.

00:03:02.299 --> 00:03:03.583
Looks like a double Whopper with cheese,

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.870
bacon, mayo, ketchup, mustard.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.990
They didn't mess with
the veggies. Thank you.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.027
You're not fooling anyone

00:03:09.027 --> 00:03:10.768
getting lettuce and onion on that one.

00:03:10.768 --> 00:03:14.140
The rodeo burger is a
little guy with onion rings.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.470
The rodeo burger. Yeehaw.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.995
On to the chicken.

00:03:17.995 --> 00:03:19.030
I'll just put this over here.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.470
Japan does not have

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.040
what we call the original
chicken sandwich.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.720
And I don't know why Burger King,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.240
maybe just to set itself apart,

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.515
the chicken sandwich is
this, like, sub shape.

00:03:28.515 --> 00:03:30.040
It's like I'm holding the phone.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:30.920
This is great.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.930
Chicken junior, spicy chicken junior.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:33.773
Let's go spicy.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:38.820
Barely registers in the spice meter.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.870
Wait!

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.703
Yeah.

00:03:40.703 --> 00:03:43.770
BKs in the US have something
called the Ch'King sandwich.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.610
You can get the sandwich
regular or deluxe.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.740
You can also get the sandwich
flavor regular or spicy.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.690
So here is the regular regular.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.723
And as you can see,

00:03:53.723 --> 00:03:56.240
just comes with sauce and
pickles and the chicken.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.410
You can get it deluxe and spicy,

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.480
so we went with deluxe,
comes with all these veggies

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.470
that you brush off right
when you start eating it,

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:07.798
and it has got a spicy kind
of hue to the chicken there.

00:04:07.798 --> 00:04:10.060
Here's our side menu.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.850
Let's start with this one.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.948
We've got hot dog.

00:04:13.948 --> 00:04:16.493
It's got such a big sausage.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.863
This one is chili beans hot dog.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.745
And next we have this little guy,

00:04:26.745 --> 00:04:28.730
snack chicken.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:32.038
And last we have this one,

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.620
chili cheese fries.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.570
And if you want some veggies,
you can order Caesar salad.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.720
But my bad, I forgot to order.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.780
Also exclusives to the US
are these, chicken fries.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.150
As you can tell, they look like fries,

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.932
but they're pieces of chicken.

00:04:47.932 --> 00:04:49.280
Not bad.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.671
You can get Mott's applesauce.

00:04:51.671 --> 00:04:53.462
Jalapeño cheddar bites.

00:04:53.462 --> 00:04:54.750
I've never heard of these.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.930
And now I know why.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:02.640
Burger King in the US has
two iced-coffee flavors,

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.990
mocha and vanilla.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.498
Assuming that's the mocha.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.513
Tastes exactly like chocolate milk.

00:05:10.513 --> 00:05:11.346
Blech! No.

00:05:11.346 --> 00:05:12.829
Oh, the aftertaste is horrible.

00:05:12.829 --> 00:05:13.860
What the hell?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.390
That's ridiculous how bad that is.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.393
And the vanilla.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.780
That is so sweet.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:22.955
I'm gonna keep this one.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.110
So, here is our dessert menus.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.568
Here we have coffee float.

00:05:28.568 --> 00:05:30.334
A little bit melting, sorry.

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:33.330
And we have melon soda float.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.660
Coke float and Coke Zero float.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:41.530
And here we've got premium
sundae chocolate and coffee.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:44.388
And here is our chocolate sundae

00:05:44.388 --> 00:05:46.200
and strawberry sundae.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.708
And my favorite is this apple pie.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.070
Desserts.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:57.693
Here in the US you can get
yourself a Hershey's sundae pie.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.050
Ugh.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.460
This one might have got a
little roughed up in transit.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.460
And in the US Burger King, you
can also get various shakes.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.450
Here we have Oreo shake,
a chocolate Oreo shake,

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.440
a chocolate shake, and a vanilla shake.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.273
All right.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.320
God, that's so good.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.545
The straight-up chocolate.

00:06:18.983 --> 00:06:20.400
Oh, man, this is trouble.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.280
Mm!

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.300
Wow, Burger King's shakes are really good.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.700
I'm assuming this is just
the straight Oreo one.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.530
Oh, my God, this is fantastic.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.660
Are we all curious what a
chocolate Oreo shake tastes like?

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.996
Wonder no more.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.900
Good. This one's the best.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.520
Also at a US Burger King, you
can get a soft-serve cone.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:44.460
I didn't get it,

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.350
only because we have no
refrigeration unit here

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:50.370
and it would just be a cone
with a puddle of ice cream. So.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.681
Victoria, please turn me
into a giant soft-serve cone.

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.640
So, here are our drinks.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.260
Let's start with this one.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.685
This one is ginger ale;

00:07:00.685 --> 00:07:02.501
and Fanta melon;

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.240
oolong tea,

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.190
which is Chinese tea;

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.006
and orange juice.

00:07:08.006 --> 00:07:11.700
And this one is Earl Grey iced tea.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.300
Next we have Darjeeling tea.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.717
And here is Calpis,

00:07:17.717 --> 00:07:21.610
which, you guys call it
Calpico in your country.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.783
But in Japan we say "ka-ru pi-su."

00:07:24.783 --> 00:07:28.090
I know it sounds like
"cow piss" in English,

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.480
but if you say Calpico to Japanese people,

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.080
they will never understand
what you're talking about.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:37.106
So in Japan, once again,
we say "ka-ru pi-su."

00:07:37.106 --> 00:07:39.798
Repeat after me. "Ka-ru pi-su."

00:07:39.798 --> 00:07:41.798
Very good!

00:07:41.798 --> 00:07:42.816
First things you can get,

00:07:42.816 --> 00:07:44.950
you can get a little orange juice guy,

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:48.780
and you can also get
Capri Sun apple juice.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.870
Shout-out to the pouch.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.310
Burger King in the US has
Coke products as well,

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.870
but we have something called
a Coke Freestyle machine.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.169
If you haven't seen it,
it's this big machine

00:07:57.169 --> 00:07:59.683
that has a bunch of
Coca-Cola-related beverages.

00:07:59.683 --> 00:08:00.720
You can mix and match them.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:03.270
Anyway, we can get Hi-C fruit punch,

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.480
Hi-C pink lemonade, Fanta
orange, Mello Yello,

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:10.660
Powerade Zero, Dr Pepper,
Barq's, diet Barq's.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.435
You can also get yourself a fat-free milk.

00:08:13.435 --> 00:08:14.268
There it is.

00:08:14.268 --> 00:08:15.890
Sweetened or unsweetened tea.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.251
I think I got the sweetened.

00:08:17.251 --> 00:08:20.270
I don't want any tea. Tea sucks.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.880
We also have something
called frozen Cokes.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.340
That is this right here.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.630
As you can see, it's
been sitting for a while,

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.500
it's starting to separate.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.650
But we have frozen Coke,

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.850
we also have a frozen Fanta wild cherry,

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.710
a frozen Fanta blue raspberry,

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.881
and a frozen strawberry lemonade.

00:08:33.881 --> 00:08:34.714
Mm.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:36.840
Oh, yeah.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.730
Japan has a few exclusives
that are similar

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.720
but different to that in the US.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:46.620
So, for example, this is
our plant-based Whopper.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:50.866
This burger is made from 100% soybeans.

00:08:50.866 --> 00:08:52.320
Itadakimasu!

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.460
It's actually delicious.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.875
I like it.

00:08:57.875 --> 00:08:58.708
Mm.

00:08:58.708 --> 00:09:01.810
When it comes to
vegetarianism and veganism,

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.740
they are not that popular in Japan.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.840
But gradually, especially
the restaurants in Tokyo

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.970
are offering more vegan
or vegetarian meals

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:12.120
because there is more Japanese people

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.220
and non-Japanese people
who are vegan or vegetarian

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.270
compared to other places in Japan.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:19.930
But overall, the vegan
or vegetarian option

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.700
is still limited in Japan.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.340
And in the US, we have
the Impossible Whopper.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.220
What's the difference?

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:28.370
Well, the Impossible burger
has all these ingredients.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.790
So as you can see, a lot more.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.987
I am curious.

00:09:32.987 --> 00:09:34.520
That looks like meat, right?

00:09:37.552 --> 00:09:38.470
Tastes exactly like a Whopper.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.950
I don't think I would
notice the difference.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.847
They're covering the
lack of meat with, like,

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.527
with that char flavor
that they have on there.

00:09:44.527 --> 00:09:46.610
Oh, it's good.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:49.010
In Japan, we call this burger

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.893
crispy chicken burger.

00:09:50.893 --> 00:09:52.580
And in the US, we have
the before-mentioned

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.730
Ch'King sandwich,

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.020
which comes in varieties
of spicy and/or deluxe.

00:09:57.020 --> 00:10:00.823
For breakfast, our hash
brown comes in one big piece.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.430
Whereas in the US,

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:05.720
our hash browns come in little bites.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:10.503
And in Japan, we have this cheese bites.

00:10:10.503 --> 00:10:11.911
Look at this.

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:14.593
And in the US, we have
eight-piece cheesy tots.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.510
And on to the US breakfast exclusives.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.260
As you can see, we have
a lot more going on

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.610
in our breakfast menu here
in the US than Japan has.

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:25.550
Here in the US, you can
get your breakfast sandwich

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.890
in biscuit or Croissan'wich options.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:31.570
Croissan'wich is, of course,
a croissant sandwich.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.940
Took those two words, put
them together. Croissan'wich.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.480
So we have bacon, egg, and cheese;

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.988
ham, egg, and cheese;

00:10:38.988 --> 00:10:42.304
and sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:10:42.304 --> 00:10:45.400
We have two breakfast burritos.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.580
The Egg-Normous breakfast burrito,

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.088
which I'm assuming is this one,

00:10:49.088 --> 00:10:51.938
'cause it is enormous.

00:10:51.938 --> 00:10:53.889
The breakfast burrito junior.

00:10:53.889 --> 00:10:55.410
Look at this little guy!

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.830
French toast sticks.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:59.280
Who doesn't like French toast?

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.070
Finally, pancake platter
with just three pancakes

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.690
or a pancake platter with three pancakes

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.523
and a side of sausage.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:11.960
The fries at Burger King in
Japan come in three sizes,

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.793
small,

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:15.633
medium,

00:11:17.216 --> 00:11:18.143
and large.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:22.750
Fries in the US at Burger
King come in four sizes,

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.330
value, small, medium, or large.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.653
Or maybe it's value, small, medium, large.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.170
Does this look right?

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.580
Any of you "Food Wars" heads

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.460
would've seen the Burger
King US vs UK episode

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.610
where we uncovered Frygate.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:41.770
Two sizes had pretty much
the exact same unit of fries.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.430
Now, as you can see from these,

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.720
I can't tell which is
the value and the small.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.330
I'm assuming this is the medium.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:53.190
Well, unfortunately, we cannot
do that amazingly accurate

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.850
scientific test that we
did in the last episode

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:58.290
because the fries have been compromised.

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:00.365
They all came in the same bag, and ...

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.581
I think they knew what we were up to

00:12:03.581 --> 00:12:06.537
and they purposely dumped
all the fries in the same bag

00:12:06.537 --> 00:12:09.800
to contaminate the experiment.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.570
You've outsmarted us this time.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:12.790
George: Let's weigh the large fries

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.503
to see how much you actually get.

00:12:15.432 --> 00:12:17.780
151 grams.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.007
What if we did a thing where, like,

00:12:19.007 --> 00:12:22.010
whatever lands and stays on counts as it?

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.430
Does that seem like a fair thing to say?

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.030
That's really smart, what
I just did there, I think.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:31.563
It's 195 grams.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.463
Let's weigh Japan's Whopper.

00:12:36.055 --> 00:12:37.630
250 grams.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:41.499
Joe: And let us weigh
our Whopper in the US.

00:12:41.499 --> 00:12:43.580
Yo!

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:44.830
270?

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.305
Yeah, 270 grams.

00:12:46.305 --> 00:12:48.250
So pretty close. Surprisingly close.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.500
If you're not feeling like having beef,

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.800
Burger King also has some chicken options.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.160
You can order your chicken nuggets

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:56.950
in five pieces and eight pieces.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.100
Here in the US, you can
get your nuggets in sizes

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:02.130
of four pieces, eight
pieces, or 16 pieces.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:05.139
And it's worth noting that
you can only get the 16-piece

00:13:05.139 --> 00:13:07.790
online or through their
app, and even if you do,

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:10.360
they still just give you two eight-pieces.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:12.000
I don't know why either.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.183
So, let's weigh eight-piece nuggets.

00:13:15.279 --> 00:13:18.130
130 grams.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:21.230
Divide by eight equals

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:25.171
16.25 grams per nugget.

00:13:25.171 --> 00:13:27.110
I don't know if we can get
as accurate of a measurement

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.030
for something so small.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.930
So we will use this guy instead.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:35.563
So I'll just do this
and put this scale here.

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:38.961
Ah!

00:13:38.961 --> 00:13:40.011
This is a bad idea.

00:13:40.011 --> 00:13:44.480
Eight pieces is 104 grams,

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:49.033
divided by eight is 13 grams.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.683
In Japan, we have three drink sizes,

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:54.583
small

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.330
and medium

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.403
and large.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.650
In the US, we have four drink sizes.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.790
Value, which only comes with a value meal;

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.090
small; medium; and large.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.980
Now, I want to note that
the US's largest drink size

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:14.735
is 112% larger than Japan's largest drink.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.380
Now, what's the biggest meal

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:21.630
you can get in Japan's Burger King?

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:25.258
Over here, it's the King Meal.

00:14:25.258 --> 00:14:29.770
[singing "Circle of Life"]

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:31.953
The King Meal ranges anywhere

00:14:31.953 --> 00:14:35.286
from 790 to 990 yen

00:14:35.286 --> 00:14:37.160
depending on the burger you choose.

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.650
It has your choice of an avocado Whopper,

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.120
double cheeseburger, or Whopper.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.410
We chose the double cheeseburger,

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.143
which comes with small fries,

00:14:47.143 --> 00:14:48.676
five-piece nuggets,

00:14:48.676 --> 00:14:51.490
medium Coke, and apple pie.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:55.140
And in the US, currently
our single biggest menu item

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:58.520
at a Burger King is the
$30 Ultimate Party Bundle.

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:00.700
Now, you could only
order this party bundle

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:04.400
through the BK app, and
it includes two Whoppers,

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.741
two double cheeseburgers,

00:15:05.741 --> 00:15:07.291
two original chicken sandwiches,

00:15:07.291 --> 00:15:09.060
two eight-piece chicken nuggets,

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.000
four small fries, and four small drinks.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.883
And it costs:

00:15:13.883 --> 00:15:15.640
$30.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.040
In Japan, a Whopper cheese set,

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.800
it costs around 890 yen, or $7.80 US.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.237
Whereas in the US, the same meal

00:15:24.237 --> 00:15:27.428
with a small fry and drink is $9.29,

00:15:27.428 --> 00:15:31.478
or 1,059.65 Japanese yen.

00:15:31.478 --> 00:15:32.340
What about the medium?

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:33.810
You get that with the
medium fry and medium drink,

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:35.401
it's $10.29,

00:15:35.401 --> 00:15:40.401
or 1,173.71 Japanese yen.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.093
What about the large?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.952
Poof! Hey, there it is,
right in front of me.

00:15:45.952 --> 00:15:49.627
Large fries and drink, $11.29,

00:15:49.627 --> 00:15:54.492
or 1,287.78 Japanese yen.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.000
Let's look at calories.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.010
In Japan, a Whopper is 676 calories.

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:04.920
The calories aren't too bad,

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:07.650
but watch out for the sodium levels.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:10.788
One Japan Whopper is 113%

00:16:10.788 --> 00:16:13.530
of your daily recommended
amount of sodium.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.196
Too much!

00:16:15.196 --> 00:16:18.420
In the US, our Whopper is 667 calories.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.380
Both Whoppers are pretty comparable

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:21.640
in most of the categories,

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.120
but there's one statistic
that really stands out,

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.380
the salt content.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:30.100
The sodium level in Japan's
Whopper is 122% higher

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.730
than that in the US.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.497
Let's make that a meal.

00:16:33.497 --> 00:16:36.110
A Whopper with large
fries and a large Coke

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:39.520
is 1,323 calories.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:44.100
And the same meal in the
US is 1,680 calories,

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.120
so a lot more.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.302
Now, a big portion of the calories

00:16:47.302 --> 00:16:49.530
actually come from the large Coke.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:53.413
The US's is roughly 182% more calories

00:16:53.413 --> 00:16:54.604
than that of Japan's.

00:16:54.604 --> 00:16:57.340
Let's look at the highest-calorie sandwich

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:58.614
at Japan's Burger King.

00:16:58.614 --> 00:17:01.372
The double Whopper cheese is here.

00:17:01.372 --> 00:17:04.960
Eating one of these is already
half of your daily calories

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.890
and a little over your
daily recommended protein.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:11.440
The main thing to watch
out for here is the sodium,

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:16.010
which is 152% of your
daily recommended value.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.960
Whereas in the US, our
highest-calorie sandwich

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:21.950
is the spicy chicken
deluxe sandwich, seen here.

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:23.200
If you're worried about your health,

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.470
steer clear of this one.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:29.180
The fat content is 190%
your daily allowance,

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:34.158
and the sodium is over 200%
of your daily allowance.

00:17:34.158 --> 00:17:35.610
Yikes.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.030
As I mentioned earlier,

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:40.050
the biggest menu item is the King Meal.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:42.917
If you get it with a
double bacon cheeseburger,

00:17:42.917 --> 00:17:46.930
the total calories are 1,329.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:50.380
That's 66% of your daily calories.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.690
And, of course, the $30
Ultimate Party Bundle,

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.930
which is 8,903 calories,

00:17:56.930 --> 00:18:00.655
or 445% your daily

00:18:00.655 --> 00:18:02.546
caloric allowance.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.208
Burger King in Japan doesn't disclose

00:18:08.208 --> 00:18:09.900
the exact ingredients,

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.200
but it does disclose where
the ingredients come from

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.630
and where they're finished processing.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:17.580
For example, the Whopper beef patties

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:21.480
are sourced from Australia,
New Zealand, and Europe,

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:23.713
but they are processed in Australia,

00:18:23.713 --> 00:18:26.272
Japan, and Austria.

00:18:26.272 --> 00:18:27.700
Burger King in the US is pretty vague

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:28.920
when it comes to its ingredients.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.980
They don't disclose a
comprehensive list anywhere.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.070
At the end of 2020,

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:36.810
Burger King permanently
banned 120 artificial flavors

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.620
from their menu, including aluminum,

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:43.120
yellows 1 through 5, BHA, and BHT.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.160
Here's the complete list.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.260
It was actually a lot of stuff.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:48.303
Good for you guys.

00:18:49.276 --> 00:18:50.109
Ow!

00:18:51.675 --> 00:18:53.049
Naotomo: Simba!

00:18:53.049 --> 00:18:54.574
Simba!

